1
00:00:02,926 --> 00:00:05,564
Meanwhile, a rival was growing.

2
00:00:05,564 --> 00:00:10,263
Pepsi-Cola was born in North
Carolina in 1898, and it went

3
00:00:10,263 --> 00:00:12,242
bankrupt more than once.

4
00:00:12,242 --> 00:00:16,055
In those hard years, Coca-Cola
reportedly had chances to buy

5
00:00:16,055 --> 00:00:18,823
Pepsi. It passed every time.

6
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:20,960
Pepsi fought back with price.

7
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,110
During the Great Depression, it sold
a twelve-ounce bottle for a

8
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:29,117
nickel. The same price as Coke's
six-and-a-half-ounce bottle.

9
00:00:29,117 --> 00:00:31,279
Coke answered with feelings.

10
00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:35,530
In 1971, it filmed young people
from around the world on a

11
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:39,817
hilltop in Italy, singing about
buying the world a Coke.

12
00:00:39,817 --> 00:00:43,415
A version of that song became
a hit on the radio.

13
00:00:43,415 --> 00:00:45,553
Pepsi answered with taste.

14
00:00:45,553 --> 00:00:50,040
In the Pepsi Challenge, which
started in 1975, people took a sip

15
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,190
from two unmarked cups...

16
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:55,400
and on camera, a lot of them picked Pepsi.

17
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,475
Coke was still bigger, but
it was losing ground.

18
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:02,463
And inside the company, someone
asked a dangerous question: what

19
00:01:02,463 --> 00:01:04,670
if we change the taste?
